na manera triste, de una manera lamentable,\ntriste\n\nSarka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsadness, grief\n \n/ tristeza, pena\n\nSarka paskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cause grief, to cause sadness, to grieve\n \n/ causar pena, causar tristeza, afligir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/19\n):\n \nNahki upla kum sip sa Gâd spiritka holikira sarka paskaia?\n \n–\n \nHow can a person grieve God’s\n\nholy spirit?\n \n/ ¿Cómo puede una persona entristecer el espíritu santo de Dios?)\n\nSarka pura luaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto overcome grief, to overcome sadness\n \n/ superar el dolor, superar la tristeza\n\nSarka tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngreat sadness\n \n/ gran tristeza\n\nSasakra\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSakaia\n\nSasibrira\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSibriaia\n\nSât\n \n(Sat)\n \n–\n \nkind, type, sort\n \n/ clase, tipo\n\n(From the English word / De la palabra inglesa:\n \nsort\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nlfb97\n):\n \nNanara Gâd upla sâtka sut ra pain kaiki ba yang tânka brisna\n \n–\n \nNow I understand that God looks favorably on all\nsorts of people (is not partial)\n \n/ Ahora entiendo que Dios mira favorablemente a todo tipo de personas (no es parcial))\n\nAl s\nȃ\nt\n \n–\n \nall sorts, all kinds\n \n/ todo tipo, toda clase\n\nKupia sâtka\n \n–\n \ntype of heart, sort of heart, heart condition\n \n/ tipo de corazón, condición del corazón\n\nSât kum\n \n(\ntc-Sandy Bay Sirpi\n)\n \n–\n \nstrange, odd, weird, rare\n \n/ extraño, raro\n\nSât sât\n \n–\n \nall sorts, all kinds\n \n/ todo tipo, toda clase\n\nIwanka tnatka sât sât\n \n–\n \nall sorts of ways of living, all sorts of customs, diverse customs\n \n/ todo tipo de\nformas de vivir, todo tipo de costumbres, costumbres diversas\n\nTnatka sât sât\n \n–\n \nall sorts of ways, all kinds of ways\n \n/ todo tipo de formas\n\nSât wala\n \n–\n \nanother kind, different\n \n/ otro tipo, diferente\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nNahki sât wala sa ki?\n \n–\n \nHow is it different?\n \n/ ¿Cómo es diferente?)\n\nSât wala daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make different, to change, to change to another kind\n \n/ hacer diferente, cambiar,\ncambiar a otro tipo\n\nSim sât\n \n–\n \nsame sort, same type, similar, similarly\n \n/ mismo tipo, similar\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nNaiwa piua ra, sim s\nâ\nt daukisa\n \n–\n \nIn our time, we do similarly\n \n/ En nuestro tiempo, hacemos lo mismo\n)\n\nSim s\nâ\nt daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do similarly, to imitate\n \n/ hacer de manera similar, imitar\n\nSatadi\n \n(a/t:\n \nSatade\n-\ndict,dictu-alt\n)\n \n–\n \nSaturday\n \n/ sábado\n\nSatil\n \n(\ndb\n,\ndictu\n,\ndict-alt\n;\n \nSadil\n-\ndict\n;\n \nSadl\n-\ndict-alt\n;\n \nSadil\n&\nSatil\n-\ndictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsaddle\n \n/ albarda, montura\n\nSatil mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto saddle\n \n/ ensillar",
